Noctalia Greeter on Void Linux
==============================

1. Point greetd at the session wrapper in /etc/greetd/config.toml:

	[default_session]
	command = "/usr/bin/noctalia-greeter-session"
	user = "_greeter"

   Void's greetd package runs its greeter as "_greeter", not "greeter".
   /var/lib/noctalia-greeter is created owned by _greeter on install.

2. Initialize greeter state (as root, once):

	GREETER_USER=_greeter noctalia-greeter-apply-appearance --setup-system

3. Enable greetd, and disable any other display manager and the agetty
   service on greetd's VT (see /usr/share/doc/greetd/README.voidlinux):

	ln -s /etc/sv/greetd /var/service/

Optional: appearance sync with Noctalia
---------------------------------------
Needs polkit (provides pkexec):

	xbps-install polkit

Each sync asks for an admin password by default. To allow a user to sync
without a password (an explicit administrator choice):

	noctalia-greeter passwordless-sync enable <user>
